  "lineage": "Early-1960s Liverpool-and-Merseyside beat-music style emerging from the convergence of skiffle, American R&B, and rock-and-roll into the canonical guitar-bass-drums-and-vocal-harmony four-piece beat-group format. The Beatles, Gerry and the Pacemakers, the Searchers, the Merseybeats, and Cilla Black constituted the canonical roster; the Cavern Club Liverpool and the Star-Club Hamburg anchored the institutional performance circuit. Distinguished from broader British Invasion by Merseybeat's Liverpool-specific geographic-cultural identity.",
